  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="6590-e8ef-799a-dbc1" name="Easy Come, Easy Go" hidden="false">
      <description>Due to their diminutive size and haphazard construction, Grot vehicles are not very resilient once properly hit and thus even a single lasgun shot can often easily dismantle them in a spectacular fashion. Any vehicle with this rule will be automatically destroyed by any glancing or penetrating hits on them. </description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="cf63-55c0-52a4-bf0d" name="Hard Targets" hidden="false">
      <description>It can be hard to pick out specific targets in a large horde of gretchins, especially since each grot will do its best to use their komrades for cover whenever possible. Any hit roll against a unit with this rule may be passed onto another unit with this rule that is within 2&quot; of it, granted it is within range and line of sight of the shooter.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ffe0-b14d-6427-027d" name="For Da Revolushun!" hidden="false">
      <description>Being incredible cowards invidually, Grots fighting for &quot;Da Revolushun!&quot; are often led by Kommissars duos that edge the other Grots on to greater feats of bravery. Grots units with Kommissars may always choose to substitute half the number of Wounds in their unit for their normal Leadership value. If a Grot unit numbers 21 or more wounds in total, it has the Fearless special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d269-9173-57fa-4cab" name="Da Red Ikon" hidden="false">
      <description>Da Red Ikon is the Ikon of Da Revolushun, and waving it around on the battlefield inspires nearby Grots with zealous frenzy. Any unit, from the same platoon as the unit including a Da Red Ikon, that is within 6&quot; have the fearless universal special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2aba-3adf-771b-701f" name="Noisemaker" hidden="false">
      <description>Attempting to block out the scary noises of battle, these Grots use a wide array of improvised instruments to loudly bolster the agressiveness of their fellow kin. Any unit, from the same platoon as the unit including a Noisemaker, that is within 6&quot; have the fleet universal special rule.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
